(1296349, 164286, 6999, '<td valign="top">Whilst I like this as a composition, it does lack a certain quality of texture. The light through that window is attractive, and lends an element of difference essential in such an obvious challenge. Good work.</td>', 'Whilst I like this as a composition, it does lack a certain quality of texture. The light through that window is attractive, and lends an element of difference essential in such an obvious challenge. Good work.', '2005-04-16 13:37:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(1296351, 164647, 6999, '<td valign="top">Seems to lack detail and resolution - which has killed a sense of texture in those bricks.</td>', 'Seems to lack detail and resolution - which has killed a sense of texture in those bricks.', '2005-04-16 13:37:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(1296353, 164281, 30896, '<td valign="top">very nice and one of few inventive ideas in this challenge, however - isn''t the line looking brand new?</td>', 'very nice and one of few inventive ideas in this challenge, however - isn''t the line looking brand new?', '2005-04-16 13:38:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(1296356, 165818, 6999, '<td valign="top">Very grey - and I can''t really see a reason for not using that range of whites above your brightest point. From the look of the shadows on the church front, there ought to be detail in those trees available, rather than a simple silhouette. If it was mood you were after, I would suggest that a greater range of contrast to bring out the clouds, and perhaps enhance some sense of texture on the boarding might have been more effective. This seems, especially as it all darker than the background on which it''s displayed, simply to be underexposed.</td>', 'Very grey - and I can''t really see a reason for not using that range of whites above your brightest point. From the look of the shadows on the church front, there ought to be detail in those trees available, rather than a simple silhouette. If it was mood you were after, I would suggest that a greater range of contrast to bring out the clouds, and perhaps enhance some sense of texture on the boarding might have been more effective. This seems, especially as it all darker than the background on which it''s displayed, simply to be underexposed.', '2005-04-16 13:40:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(1296367, 165262, 6999, '<td valign="top">Obviously, to maintain any detail in that frontage, you had to over-expose the sky; nevertheless, that over-exposure is not helping this image for me - I would rather in fact that the entire sky was blown out. That said, there is good sense of texture and detail and tone in the building. Difficult, without knowing your equipment, expertise, or intent, to recommend the best approach to fix this.</td>', 'Obviously, to maintain any detail in that frontage, you had to over-expose the sky; nevertheless, that over-exposure is not helping this image for me - I would rather in fact that the entire sky was blown out. That said, there is good sense of texture and detail and tone in the building. Difficult, without knowing your equipment, expertise, or intent, to recommend the best approach to fix this.', '2005-04-16 13:49:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(1296376, 165271, 6999, '<td valign="top">Very very interesting approach - arresting, in fact, as it has stopped me from expiring with boredom after the last twenty or so images. Excellent compositionally, good spread of tonality, and yet still easy on the eye. I would wish for a more intense level of detail, to bring this neo-modernist kind of composition more comfortably into a real world - it might add some depth to the overall view of this, rather than what I''m finding quite a simple image. Simple but good, that is. I''m intrigued to see whose this is.</td>', 'Very very interesting approach - arresting, in fact, as it has stopped me from expiring with boredom after the last twenty or so images. Excellent compositionally, good spread of tonality, and yet still easy on the eye. I would wish for a more intense level of detail, to bring this neo-modernist kind of composition more comfortably into a real world - it might add some depth to the overall view of this, rather than what I''m finding quite a simple image. Simple but good, that is. I''m intrigued to see whose this is.', '2005-04-16 13:53:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(1296389, 165037, 34836, '<td valign="top">Very good composition.  It''s too bad the sun is so bright.  I really like this one.</td>', 'Very good composition.  It''s too bad the sun is so bright.  I really like this one.', '2005-04-16 14:00:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(1296401, 164828, 29474, '<td valign="top">The wonderful colours take the focus away from the building.</td>', 'The wonderful colours take the focus away from the building.', '2005-04-16 14:08:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(1296441, 165659, 31214, '<td valign="top">Looks like a giant monster hiding in the tree!  I like the late afternoon sun.</td>', 'Looks like a giant monster hiding in the tree!  I like the late afternoon sun.', '2005-04-16 14:39:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(1296443, 165026, 31214, '<td valign="top">Image works well with black and white.  Good job.</td>', 'Image works well with black and white.  Good job.', '2005-04-16 14:40:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(1296447, 164385, 31214, '<td valign="top">Nice composition.  Focus perhaps a little soft.  Nice sky.</td>', 'Nice composition.  Focus perhaps a little soft.  Nice sky.', '2005-04-16 14:42:02.000000', NULL, 1),
