(1308080, 166079, 19708, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by GeneralE:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by BradP:</b></div><hr/><i> A touch of humor at last!<br/>Well seen and an unusual take on this challenge. Not sure if the building is abandoned or the field is, but regardless, the fencing seems to be taking top honors as a focal point instead of a building. Image is a bit soft/needing to be a bit sharper/clearer. (4) </i></td></tr></table> <br/>I see the gate itself as abandoned, as evidenced by the lack of a fence on the one side. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Ahhh.... but is a gate a building? You knew you would get hammered submitting this didn''t you (BTDT) :P<br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by GeneralE:</b></div><hr/><i>-- I forgot to use it for the last "Humor" challenge.</i></td></tr></table> <br/>Goofball!<br/>:)</td>', 'Originally posted by GeneralE: Originally posted by BradP: A touch of humor at last!Well seen and an unusual take on this challenge. Not sure if the building is abandoned or the field is, but regardless, the fencing seems to be taking top honors as a focal point instead of a building. Image is a bit soft/needing to be a bit sharper/clearer. (4)  I see the gate itself as abandoned, as evidenced by the lack of a fence on the one side.  Ahhh.... but is a gate a building? You knew you would get hammered submitting this didn''t you (BTDT) :POriginally posted by GeneralE:-- I forgot to use it for the last "Humor" challenge. Goofball!:)', '2005-04-20 13:47:28.000000', NULL, 0),
