(1308168, 164633, 33736, '<td valign="top">Reading a couple of other comments reminds me of how important details are in planned shots.  For example, I could tell how many members were way too young to remember the 70''s ("clean" and "neat" were not characteristics of the hippie culture!)  <br/> <br/>You have a good eye - but need to be aware of those things we nitpickers find distracting. :-)     <br/> <br/>But, no matter how careful you are, there''s always a sharp eye like Goodman, who noticed that those very new, very shiny shoes were on the wrong feet!  Funny, man.</td>', 'Reading a couple of other comments reminds me of how important details are in planned shots.  For example, I could tell how many members were way too young to remember the 70''s ("clean" and "neat" were not characteristics of the hippie culture!)   You have a good eye - but need to be aware of those things we nitpickers find distracting. :-)      But, no matter how careful you are, there''s always a sharp eye like Goodman, who noticed that those very new, very shiny shoes were on the wrong feet!  Funny, man.', '2005-04-20 14:23:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(1308174, 166094, 31409, '<td valign="top">Thanks for your constructive criticism and compliments. This was a few moments after a torrential downpour, and the white specks are actually ice pellets/mini hail, I can now see why others thought it was overprocessed and looked speckled. The building was actually constructed like that, I didn''t add two pictures together. I had thought about cropping the light pole but was afraid it would be seen as removing a major element and I didn''t want a disqualification.</td>', 'Thanks for your constructive criticism and compliments. This was a few moments after a torrential downpour, and the white specks are actually ice pellets/mini hail, I can now see why others thought it was overprocessed and looked speckled. The building was actually constructed like that, I didn''t add two pictures together. I had thought about cropping the light pole but was afraid it would be seen as removing a major element and I didn''t want a disqualification.', '2005-04-20 14:24:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(1308202, 165776, 28742, '<td valign="top">This was great. A 7 from me - only real detractor was that hot spot at the top-middle. As far as my idea of "meets the challenge" a 10++++ :)</td>', 'This was great. A 7 from me - only real detractor was that hot spot at the top-middle. As far as my idea of "meets the challenge" a 10++++ :)', '2005-04-20 14:37:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(1308217, 165661, 19708, '<td valign="top">Ah - now I see what happened.<br/>Recent PC upgrade/hardware changes.<br/>Video setting was at 16 Bit color, not 32 Bit.<br/>Was seeing some "odd" banding in a number of my other portfolio pics and had me wondering. Now at 32 Bit, it''s back the way it should have been.</td>', 'Ah - now I see what happened.Recent PC upgrade/hardware changes.Video setting was at 16 Bit color, not 32 Bit.Was seeing some "odd" banding in a number of my other portfolio pics and had me wondering. Now at 32 Bit, it''s back the way it should have been.', '2005-04-20 14:41:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(1308308, 164625, 27574, '<td valign="top">Very nice image and composition and no "obnoxiously distracting white border"!! :)  Very good tones and contrast</td>', 'Very nice image and composition and no "obnoxiously distracting white border"!! :)  Very good tones and contrast', '2005-04-20 15:06:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(1308353, 166079, 1031, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by BradP:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by GeneralE:</b></div><hr/><i>I see the gate itself as abandoned, as evidenced by the lack of a fence on the one side. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Ahhh.... but is a gate a building? You knew you would get hammered submitting this didn''t you (BTDT) :P</i></td></tr></table> <br/>Someone built it, I think : ) Of course I knew ...<br/>And it''s not all <u>that</u> blurry considering I was driving by at about 35 mph at the time ...</td>', 'Originally posted by BradP: Originally posted by GeneralE:I see the gate itself as abandoned, as evidenced by the lack of a fence on the one side.  Ahhh.... but is a gate a building? You knew you would get hammered submitting this didn''t you (BTDT) :P Someone built it, I think : ) Of course I knew ...And it''s not all that blurry considering I was driving by at about 35 mph at the time ...', '2005-04-20 15:18:55.000000', NULL, 0),
