(1311397, 165167, 31637, '<td valign="top">nice finish Cheryl. Your starting to get good. I like this, it''s a great structure for the challenge. I think you could of left the color..maybe might of looked even better! good clarity and angle.</td>', 'nice finish Cheryl. Your starting to get good. I like this, it''s a great structure for the challenge. I think you could of left the color..maybe might of looked even better! good clarity and angle.', '2005-04-21 17:16:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(1311602, 165733, 17126, '<td valign="top">I am astounded that this is last place out of almost 500 entries. I really expected the brown ribbon to be a ridiculous picture, but I think this one would be justified in being in, say, the top 20%.<br/> <br/>Wow. I''m actually speechless.</td>', 'I am astounded that this is last place out of almost 500 entries. I really expected the brown ribbon to be a ridiculous picture, but I think this one would be justified in being in, say, the top 20%. Wow. I''m actually speechless.', '2005-04-21 18:56:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(1311717, 165901, 35739, '<td valign="top">Beautiful Photo!</td>', 'Beautiful Photo!', '2005-04-21 19:44:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(1311871, 166037, 6306, '<td valign="top">I love the composition of this photograph. Great work.</td>', 'I love the composition of this photograph. Great work.', '2005-04-21 20:54:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(1312190, 166097, 31637, '<td valign="top">I like the oversharpening here...for some reason, I do the same with my photos...and I like the effect here...good composition...you might of been able to fit the whole building in the frame..im not sure because Im not familiar with it. But the clarity is great and this angle is a good one. You should try getting "lower" if you notice with most of my shots, they are always taken from 2 ft from the ground...I keep my tripod really low...try it out in compositions like this..get close and low and get some sky with your subject as well!</td>', 'I like the oversharpening here...for some reason, I do the same with my photos...and I like the effect here...good composition...you might of been able to fit the whole building in the frame..im not sure because Im not familiar with it. But the clarity is great and this angle is a good one. You should try getting "lower" if you notice with most of my shots, they are always taken from 2 ft from the ground...I keep my tripod really low...try it out in compositions like this..get close and low and get some sky with your subject as well!', '2005-04-21 22:45:36.000000', NULL, 0),
